<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-21135] ldiskfs: mb_groups reads wrong group descriptor, ldiskfs_error() on last group (6.10+)</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21135</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Reported by Chris Walker.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Reading /proc/fs/ldiskfs/&amp;lt;dev&amp;gt;/mb_groups on a 6.10+ kernel triggers ldiskfs_error() for the last group. With errors=panic the server panics; otherwise the journal is aborted and the target is remounted read-only.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="preformattedContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;LDISKFS-fs error (device dm-1): ldiskfs_get_group_desc:280: comm cat: block_group &amp;gt;= groups_count - block_group = 4, groups_count = 4
LDISKFS-fs (dm-1): Remounting filesystem read-only
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In the field this was seen as:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="preformattedContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;LDISKFS-fs error (device nvme1n1): ldiskfs_get_group_desc:280: comm grep: block_group &amp;gt;= groups_count - block_group = 6400, groups_count = 6400
Aborting journal on device nvme1n1-8.
Kernel panic - not syncing: LDISKFS-fs (device nvme1n1): panic forced after error
 ldiskfs_handle_error.cold+0x13/0x13 [ldiskfs]
 __ldiskfs_error+0xed/0x160 [ldiskfs]
 ldiskfs_get_group_desc+0x78/0xb0 [ldiskfs]
 ldiskfs_mb_seq_groups_show+0x46/0x210 [ldiskfs]
 seq_read_iter+0x26f/0x3f0
 proc_reg_read_iter+0x43/0x80
 vfs_read+0x205/0x320
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;a name="Rootcause"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Root cause&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The mb_groups seq_file iterator passes v = group + 1, and ext4_mb_seq_groups_show() does group-- before using it. When ext4-mballoc-extra-checks.patch was ported to 6.10 (&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-16350" title="Updated server support for new linux releases" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-16350"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-16350&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, commit cb8761fa4e), the ext4_get_group_desc() call was moved into the variable declaration, i.e. before the group--:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="code panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="codeContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre class="code-java"&gt;	ext4_group_t group = (ext4_group_t) ((unsigned &lt;span class="code-object"&gt;long&lt;/span&gt;) v);
	struct ext4_group_desc *gdp = ext4_get_group_desc(sb, group, NULL);
	...
	&lt;span class="code-keyword"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; (gdp)
		free = ext4_free_group_clusters(sb, gdp);

	group--;
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;As a result:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;the "gfree" column of row N shows the descriptor free count of group N+1;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;the last row looks up group == groups_count, which fails the bounds check in ext4_get_group_desc() and calls ext4_error().&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;p&gt;All older versions of the patch (rhel8/9, ubuntu, linux-5.x, 6.1, 6.6) do the lookup after group-- and are not affected.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Affected patches and series:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;linux-6.10/ext4-mballoc-extra-checks.patch: 6.10-ml, 6.11-ml, 6.12-ml, 6.12-rhel10.0, 6.12-rhel10.1&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;linux-6.15/ext4-mballoc-extra-checks.patch: 6.18-ml, 6.12-rhel10.2 (added in &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-19135" title="ldiskfs updates for next LTS" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-19135"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-19135&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;linux-6.19/ext4-mballoc-extra-checks.patch: 7.0-ml, 7.0.0-14-ubuntu26 (added in &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-19250" title="Support for ldiskfs kernel 7.0" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-19250"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-19250&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;h3&gt;&lt;a name="Reproducer"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Reproducer&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;On any 6.10+ ldiskfs MDT/OST:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="preformattedContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;cat /proc/fs/ldiskfs/*/mb_groups &amp;gt; /dev/null; dmesg | grep groups_count
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;a name="Fix"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Fix&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Declare gdp without initialising it and do the lookup after group--, as the pre-6.10 patches do:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="code panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="codeContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre class="code-java"&gt;	group--;
	gdp = ext4_get_group_desc(sb, group, NULL);
	&lt;span class="code-keyword"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; (gdp)
		free = ext4_free_group_clusters(sb, gdp);
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</description>
